<title>POLAND: Polifarbs, extend surge.</title>
<headline>Polifarbs, extend surge.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish paintmakers Polifarb Cieszyn and Polifarb Wroclaw extended Friday's surge, rising 9.4 and 9.9 percent to 17.4 and 16.6 zlotys respectively on their merger plan announced on Thursday, traders said.</p>
<p>Polifarb Cieszyn traded in a 3.9-million-zloty turnover and Polifarb Wroclaw in 2.7-million-zloty turnover.</p>
<p>Traders said, however, that they expected the stocks to slow their growth in the next sessions.</p>
<p>&quot;It's certainly good news (about the merger) but they can't keep soaring for so long and some investors will most likely want to take profits,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>But others said the stocks could rise to 18 or 19 zlotys.</p>
<p>On Friday Cieszyn rose 9.7 percent and Wroclaw 9.4 percent. --- Warsaw Newsroom+48 22 653 9700</p>
